# Supply-chain hygiene

Do not add runtime or build dependencies without user awareness. Prefer the standard library and existing stack.

Pin versions and use lockfiles when adding packages. Avoid floating `@latest` in production paths.

Do not pipe remote scripts (`curl | bash`, `wget | sh`) without explicit user approval and URL review.

Do not disable dependency scanning (Snyk, Dependabot, npm audit, and similar) without documented justification.

Verify package names and publishers; treat typosquat and unexpected transitive upgrades as risks.
